BT /F1 10 Tf 54 730 Td 13 TL
(Quantum Electrodynamics of Bound States in Strong Coulomb Fields) Tj T*
(J. R. Oppenheimer and H. A. Bethe - Institute for Advanced Study) Tj T*
(Abstract) Tj T*
(We calculate radiative corrections to electron binding energies in high-Z hydrogenic ions.) Tj T*
(Section 1: Introduction and Field Equations) Tj T*
(The Dirac Hamiltonian in an external four-vector potential A_mu is defined as:) Tj T*
(H_D = alpha * \(p - e A\) + beta m + e A_0) Tj T*
(The relativistic S-matrix expansion yields the self-energy operator Sigma\(p\):) Tj T*
(Sigma\(p\) = -i e^2 int d^4k / \(2 pi\)^4 gamma^mu S_F\(p - k\) gamma_mu D_F\(k\)) Tj T*
(Section 2: Vacuum Polarization Tensor) Tj T*
(The regularized polarization tensor Pi^{mu nu}\(q\) satisfies current conservation:) Tj T*
(q_mu Pi^{mu nu}\(q\) = 0) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 320 730 Td 13 TL
(Figure 1 \(Page 1\): Feynman diagram for one-loop electron self-energy and vertex correction.) Tj T*
(Section 3: Radiative Shift Calculations) Tj T*
(The Lamb shift energy difference Delta E_L is given by:) Tj T*
(Delta E_L = \(alpha / pi\) * \(Z alpha\)^4 * \(m / n^3\) * F\(Z alpha\)) Tj T*
(Table 1: Theoretical vs experimental binding energies in eV for Z=92 uranium.) Tj T*
(State | Dirac Energy \(eV\) | Self Energy \(eV\) | Net Bound Energy \(eV\)) Tj T*
(1s1/2 | -132279.9 | +355.1 | -131924.8) Tj T*
(2s1/2 | -33069.9 | +58.3 | -33011.6) Tj T*
(Figure 2 \(Page 1\): Comparison of calculated self-energy shifts across nuclear charge Z.) Tj T*
(Section 4: Concluding Remarks and Higher Order Perturbation) Tj T*
(Higher-order loop corrections remain perturbative even in the critical field regime.) Tj T*
